        "committer": {
          "name": "Timothy Day",
          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-21 15:34:49.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20232 build: dkms-deb should only build dkms packages",
        "message": "LU-20232 build: dkms-deb should only build dkms packages\n\nMake the lustre-client-modules-dkms package Architecture: all,\nsince the DKMS package ships source and builds modules on the\ntarget host rather than shipping prebuilt binaries.\n\nBuild only the arch-independent packages (source + DKMS) for\nthe dkms-debs target by passing -g to dpkg-buildpackage, and\ntrim the mv list to the packages that are actually produced.\n\nNeither package needs a configured or built tree: both ship the\nsource as-is, and the UAPI headers the DKMS package installs are\nnot generated. Copy them with dh_install instead of running a\nfull \"make install\" into a temporary DESTDIR, which compiled the\nwhole tree under fakeroot just to extract a few headers. With\nthat, build-indep is empty, the source and DKMS binary rules no\nlonger depend on configure-stamp, and the systemd and int_o2ib\nbuild profiles only consumed by configure are dropped from the\ndkms-debs target.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testgroup=full-dkms\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I287da7cff8e743b84e7e5d7f1344bdcee325db1c\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
